  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8503.01 Obtaining a Blue Envelope",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8503.01 Obtaining a Blue Envelope.\n\n(a) The following people may apply to the blue envelope program:\n\n(1) A driver licensed in New Hampshire and diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or trauma and stressor related disorder;\n\n(2) A parent applying on behalf of a minor driver licensed in New Hampshire and diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or trauma and stressor related disorder; or\n\n(3) A guardian applying on behalf of a driver licensed in New Hampshire and diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or trauma and stressor related disorder.\n\n(b) The DMSV 653 “Blue Envelope Request Form” (rev 07/26) may be obtained from www.dmv.nh.gov/forms; or in person, during business hours, from the DMV locations listed at www.dmv.nh.gov/hours-and-locations.\n\n(c) To receive a blue envelope a person can submit a completed DSMV 653 “Blue Envelope Request Form” (rev 7/26) signed by a doctor. But if they have already completed and submitted a DSMV 643 “Medically Recognized Disorder Indication” (rev 07/26) form which was signed by a doctor and is on file with the DMV, then they just need to request in person, orally, to be issued a blue envelope and they will be given on based on the DSMV 643 (rev 07/26) complying with this part.\n\n(d) A parent or legal guardian requestor applying on behalf of a participating person, shall submit a completed form DMSV 653 “Blue Envelope Request Form” (rev 07/26); and\n\n(1) To receive a blue envelope a person can submit a completed DSMV 653 “Blue Envelope Request Form” (rev 07/26) signed by a doctor. But if they have already completed and submitted a DSMV 643 “Medically Recognized Disorder Indication” (rev 07/26) form which was signed by a doctor and is on file with the DMV, then they just need to request in person, orally, to be issued a blue envelope and they will be given on based on the DSMV 643 (rev 07/26) complying with this part. ;\n\n(2) Sign the form under penalty of unsworn falsification pursuant to RSA 641:3; and\n\n(3) Include the following documentation where applicable:\n\na. If the applicant is a parent of a minor, include a copy of one of the following:\n\n1. The minor’s birth certificate;\n\n2. Certificate of adoption; or\n\n3. Adoption decree; or\n\nb. If the applicant is a legal guardian, include a copy of the order appointing the guardianship identifying the powers granted to the legal guardian.\n\n(e) Participants shall submit completed requests by:\n\n(1) Mailing to:\n\nDivision of Motor Vehicles\n\nAttn: Blue Envelope\n\n27 Hazen Drive\n\nConcord, NH 03305;\n\n(2) Hand delivering during business hours to:\n\nDivision of Motor Vehicles\n\n27 Hazen Drive\n\nConcord, NH 03305; or\n\na. Any DMV location at www.dmv.nh.gov/hours-and-locations.\n\nSource. #14643, INTERIM, eff 7-3-26, EXPIRES: 12-30-26",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8500.html"
}
